-- title:
--   Integral reduced norms give a rank-four lattice of discriminant ‖16‖qᵥ⁻²
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ and $L$ be number fields with $L$ an algebra over $K$ of degree $\operatorname{finrank}_K L = 2$, let $\sigma$ be a $K$-algebra automorphism of $L$ such that every $K$-automorphism $\tau$ of $L$ lies in the subgroup of integral powers of $\sigma$, and let $v$ be a nonzero prime of $\mathcal{O}_K$ with completion $K_v =$ `v.adicCompletion K`, valuation ring $\mathcal{O}_v =$ `v.adicCompletionIntegers K` and residue degree $\operatorname{absNorm}(v)$. Put $E_v = L \otimes_K K_v$, and let $\delta \in \mathrm{GL}_2(E_v)$. Write $D =$ `twistedCommutant K L (v.adicCompletion K) σ δ` for the $K$-subalgebra of $M_2(E_v)$ consisting of those $X$ with $X\delta = \delta\,(\sigma \otimes \mathrm{id})(X)$, the twist being applied entrywise. Assume: there are $e_1,\dots,e_4 \in M_2(E_v)$ such that a matrix $X$ lies in $D$ exactly when $X = \sum_i (e_i)\cdot(1 \otimes a_i)$ (entrywise right multiplication) for a unique vector $a \in K_v^4$; every nonzero element of $D$ is an invertible matrix; and $\tau : E_v \to K_v$ is an additive map with $\tau(l \otimes a) = \mathrm{Tr}_{L/K}(l)\,a$ for $l \in L$, $a \in K_v$. Then there exist $f_1,\dots,f_4 \in M_2(E_v)$ such that, first, a matrix $X$ belongs to the additive subgroup of $M_2(E_v)$ generated by the matrices $(f_i)\cdot(1 \otimes a)$ with $a \in \mathcal{O}_v$ if and only if $X \in D$ and $\det X = 1 \otimes a$ for some $a \in \mathcal{O}_v$; and second, $$\bigl\|\det\bigl(\tau(\mathrm{tr}(f_i f_j))\bigr)_{i,j}\bigr\| \cdot \operatorname{absNorm}(v)^2 = \|16\|,$$ the norms being those of $K_v$.
--
--   This is the local statement, at a place $v$ where the $\sigma$-twisted commutant of $\delta$ is a division quaternion algebra over $K_v$, that the elements of integral reduced norm form an $\mathcal{O}_v$-order free of rank four whose discriminant for the form $(X,Y) \mapsto \tau(\mathrm{tr}(XY)) = 2\,\mathrm{trd}(XY)$ has absolute value $\|16\|\,q_v^{-2}$, i.e. the maximal order of the ramified quaternion algebra has reduced discriminant $v$. It feeds the index computation [`AutomorphicForm.absNorm_sq_mul_relIndex_sq_mul_norm_det_trace_eq_norm_sixteen_mul_relIndex_sq_of_forall_isUnit`](thm.html#AutomorphicForm.absNorm_sq_mul_relIndex_sq_mul_norm_det_trace_eq_norm_sixteen_mul_relIndex_sq_of_forall_isUnit).
